#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/08-regular-expressions.md:125
msgid "Patterns use many backslashes: `\\d`, `\\.`, `\\s`. In a normal string, Python itself reads some backslash pairs first (`\\n` is a new line, `\\b` a backspace). A **raw string** `r\"...\"` gives every backslash to the `re` module unchanged:"
